# Release-profile hipcc flags for the AMD build (RDNA2/3/4, Linux).
# One flag per line. Text from '#' to end of line is a comment; blank lines are
# ignored. Read by build_solver.sh (release profile) and build_pool_miner.sh.
# TARI_ARCH_FLAGS, when non-empty, replaces this list.
#
# Intentionally empty: the AMD build uses the kernel defaults (including 50
# trim rounds) until a tuning sweep on AMD hardware picks a flag set
# (docs/amd-validation.md).
#
# WARP_DST_ATOMICS defaults to 0 under HIP (mean_c29.cu): the emulated
# __match_any_sync in gpu_compat.h is a ballot loop that costs about 32
# serialized cross-lane round trips per bucket store in rounds 0 to 3, and
# with 14-bit buckets it almost never finds two lanes to merge. Measured
# neutral on a Radeon AI PRO R9700 (4.2 g/s either way against 12.4 g/s for
# lolMiner): the Round kernels are bound by their scattered 8-byte bucket
# stores, which no option here changes. Full numbers, the sweep of the other
# options and the fix they point at: docs/amd_results_2026-10-28.md.
#
# Shared memory: an AMD workgroup has 64 KB. The defaults fit. Two options can
# exceed it, and the HIP build rejects them at compile time:
#   ROUND0_DST_HASH_DYNAMIC_BITS above 12 (12 needs 57,348 bytes)
#   LATE_ROUND_BPB=8 (65,540 bytes; 2 and 4 fit)
# TRIM_CUDA_GRAPH is not supported by the HIP build.
